# Dockerfile.dockerignore -- RAMEAU portal build context
#
# Context root: services/portal/ in this repository (the app root, not the repo root).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FILENAME IS LOAD-BEARING, AND IT WAS WRONG UNTIL 2026-11-02
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker reads an ignore-file from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, or as
# `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile -- and nowhere else. This file lives
# in deploy/images/portal/ while the context is services/portal/, so for as long as it was
# named plain `.dockerignore` it was read by NOTHING and every pattern below was inert:
# node_modules/, dist/ and the stale `index-*.js` build output were all uploaded with the
# context.
#
# This image escaped the worst of that only by luck. Its Dockerfile COPYs an explicit list
# rather than a wildcard, so a planted `index-stale.js` reached neither stage because no COPY
# names it -- whereas the router's `COPY *.py ./` had nothing bounding it. Luck is not the
# design this file describes, and `public/` and `src/` are copied wholesale, which only this
# list bounds.
#
# So do not rename this file back, and do not move it without moving the Dockerfile with it.
# `git mv`-ing either one alone disarms this entire file, silently.
#
# Deny-by-default, then re-admit. Same two syntax rules as the router's list: a '#' is a
# comment only at the start of a line, so never put one after a pattern; and a negation
# cannot re-admit a file whose parent directory is still excluded.

# ---- deny everything, then re-admit ----
**

# ---- the reproducible install ----
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# ---- the Vite entry and its config ----
!index.html
!vite.config.js

# ---- sources and static assets ----
!src/
!src/**
!public/
!public/**

# ---- the nginx config, copied into the serve stage as a template ----
!nginx.conf

# ---- STALE BUILD OUTPUT: never admit ----
# A committed index-*.js / index-*.css pair existed at the app root of the source tree this
# came from, while .gitignore ignored `dist`. Vite writes to dist/, so those files were a
# PREVIOUS build output, not an input. Reaching the build stage they would be harmless;
# reaching the serve stage they would shadow the fresh bundle and the portal would serve a
# stale build under a stale asset hash -- silently, with no error anywhere. Excluded by `**`
# already, and named here so that a future edit re-admitting the app root cannot sweep them
# back in.
#
# PART OF THIS BLOCK IS ROOT-ANCHORED AND PART IS NOT, and the split is the point --
# corrected 2026-11-03, because one justification had been stretched over four patterns that
# do not share it.
#
# `assets/` STAYS ROOT-ANCHORED. Recursive, it would exclude `public/assets/`, an ordinary
# place for static files that Vite copies into `dist/`; this release set carries nine .woff2
# faces, and a probe confirms `public/assets/font.woff2` survives only because of this.
#
# THE OTHER THREE ARE NOW RECURSIVE, and the previous comment was wrong to cover them with
# the same sentence. An `index-<hash>.js` is a build OUTPUT shape, never a Vite input, so
# recursion costs nothing there -- whereas root-anchoring cost plenty. Measured on this
# file AS IT STOOD BEFORE 04a4eb1 -- it is byte-identical from 1d69a59 through
# 5bb4983, so any of those five commits shows the same bytes. A reader testing the
# current file will and should see the opposite: `public/index-a1b2c3.js`,
# `public/assets/index-a1b2c3.js`, `public/assets/index-a1b2c3.css`,
# `public/assets/nested/index-deep.js` and `public/dist/index-a1b2c3.js` were all admitted.
# `public/` copies verbatim into `dist/`, so those land at the document root AND in
# `dist/assets/`, the exact directory Vite writes the real bundle into -- a stale bundle
# shadowing a fresh one, which is the harm the previous comment named and then failed to
# prevent.
#
# SCOPED TO `public/` RATHER THAN FULLY RECURSIVE, which is a deliberate narrowing of what
# the 2026-11-03 review proposed, accepted by it on the pricing below. `**/index-*.js` would
# also exclude `src/index-helpers.js` -- the pattern is `index-*`, not `index-<hash>`, and a
# hyphenated module name under `src/` is perfectly ordinary. A file of that name under `src/`
# reaches only the BUILD stage and can only reach the document root by being imported, at
# which point Vite renames it and it is a real module somebody wants.
#
# THE COST THIS DOES INCUR, stated rather than asserted away. `public/` carries no
# `index-*.js` THIS RELEASE SHIPS -- which is not the same as none being legitimate, and an
# earlier draft of this comment claimed the stronger thing. A hand-written
# `public/index-legacy.js` would now be dropped SILENTLY and show up as a 404 at runtime
# rather than as a build failure. That is the one real price of the narrowing, it is the same
# shape as the `public/assets/` font above, and it is why this is scoped to a directory whose
# contents the release controls rather than applied to `src/`.
assets/
index-*.js
index-*.css
public/**/index-*.js
public/**/index-*.css
**/dist/

# ---- the four runtime JSON files: NEVER, and at any depth ----
# Added 2026-11-03. The portal has no business carrying them, and on this image the
# consequence is worse than on the router: `public/` copies verbatim into `dist/`, which the
# serve stage copies into the nginx document root, so fleet detail under `public/` would be
# SERVED. Measured on this file AS IT STOOD BEFORE 04a4eb1 -- it is byte-identical
# from 1d69a59 through 5bb4983, so any of those five shows the same bytes:
# `public/fleet_config.json`, `public/bifrost_shell_policy.json` and
# `src/capability_registry.json` were all admitted. THE CURRENT FILE ADMITS NONE OF THE
# THREE -- the four patterns immediately below are what changed that, so a reader who tests
# HEAD will see the opposite and should.
# Named one by one rather than as `**/*.json`, which would sit below `!package.json` and
# `!package-lock.json` above and deny the portal its own manifest.
**/fleet_config.json
**/capability_registry.json
**/capability_profiles.json
**/bifrost_shell_policy.json

# ---- never, under any circumstances ----
# THIS BLOCK'S GUARANTEE RESTS ON THREE PROPERTIES, AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS GATED.
#   REACH     -- the patterns are recursive, so they apply inside `src/` and `public/`,
#                which this file re-admits wholesale.   Fixed 1d69a59. NOT gated: the
#                probes that measured it were throwaway stub contexts built outside git
#                and discarded, and no step builds a context or tests admission.
#   FINALITY  -- nothing re-admits below this block, because a .dockerignore is
#                last-match-wins.                       Fixed and GATED in 04a4eb1.
#   SHAPE COVERAGE -- the shapes listed below are the ones worth denying. NOT gated, and
#                resting on prose. The heading says "never, under any circumstances" and
#                what follows is about a dozen shapes, which is a weaker thing than the
#                heading claims. This repository's own .gitignore names shapes this list
#                does not, and `docker build` reads the WORKING TREE rather than the index,
#                so a gitignored credential is invisible to every git-based gate here and
#                still enters the image. Recorded in RELEASE-SCOPE.md as the top residual
#                risk rather than patched in passing, because closing it is a decision
#                about what this list is FOR.
#
# ONE OF THREE, NOT TWO. This heading said "ONLY TWO OF THEM ARE GATED" until 2026-11-03,
# and that was false when written: only FINALITY has a step behind it. REACH rests on
# probes that no longer exist anywhere, which is the same "promise rather than property"
# this block was added to be candid about -- found inside the note about that defect.
#
# RECURSIVE (`**/`), and on this image that matters more than on the router's. `src/**` and
# `public/**` above are wholesale re-admissions, and a root-anchored pattern cannot reach
# into either: Docker matches against the whole context-relative path and a single `*` does
# not cross a `/`, so `*.pem` matches `foo.pem` and NOT `public/foo.pem`.
#
# WHY IT IS WORSE HERE. Vite copies `public/` verbatim into `dist/`, and the Dockerfile's
# serve stage does `COPY --from=build /app/dist/ /usr/share/nginx/html/`. So a key under
# `public/` does not merely enter the build context -- it is SERVED OVER HTTP by nginx.
#
# MEASURED in a throwaway stub context built outside git and discarded. With the previous
# root-anchored set, `public/leaked.pem`, `public/leaked.key` and `src/leaked.key` all
# arrived in the built image while `root.pem` was correctly excluded; so did
# `src/BifrostPortal_fixed.jsx` and `src/BifrostPortal_v2.jsx`, which defeats the two
# stale-copy patterns entirely -- an editor's `_fixed` copy lives in `src/`, next to the
# original, which is the only place those patterns were ever meant to guard and the one
# place they did not reach. With the recursive set below all of those are excluded and
# `public/logo.svg`, `src/main.jsx`, `index.html`, `nginx.conf`, `package.json` and
# `vite.config.js` still arrive. `**/X` was confirmed to subsume `X`, so no root-anchored
# twin is kept beside it.
#
# The credential shapes are now the same set as the router's list. They diverged for no
# recorded reason, and a context that admits `public/` wholesale has more need of them, not
# less.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
**/.netrc
**/.git-credentials
**/.git/
**/.github/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
**/node_modules/
**/*.log
**/*.bak
**/*.bak-*
**/*_fixed.jsx
**/*_v2.jsx

# ---- WIDENED 2026-11-03 to the shapes this repository's own .gitignore names ----
# On John's ruling in chat, 2026-11-03, verbatim: *"2. widen to the portal"*. This is the
# portal's half of N1. The router's list follows, because the two credential sets are
# meant to be the SAME set and the note above records that they once diverged for no
# reason anyone wrote down.
#
# DERIVED BY MEASUREMENT, not by reading the list and thinking of more. Every pattern
# below is a line of `.gitignore`'s "environment and secrets", "keys and certificates"
# and "tokens" sections that had no `**/` twin in this block -- twenty-four of them,
# counted by comparing the two files line by line. Nothing here is a shape `.gitignore`
# does not already refuse to stage.
#
# CHECKED AGAINST THE TRACKED SET FIRST: none of the twenty-four matches any of the
# repository's tracked files, so none denies this build something it needs. That test is
# WEAK and says so -- the release source has not landed in this tree yet, so the strong
# version of it cannot be run today. Which is the reason the coverage is now GATED in CI
# rather than left resting on this comment.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, and the reason is the build CONTEXT. compose builds this
# image with `context: ../services/portal`, so every pattern in this file is relative to
# `services/portal/`. `.gitignore`'s assembly class -- `_scrub/`, `_preimages/`,
# `_defect-fixes/`, `WIPE-LEDGER.md` -- lives at the REPOSITORY ROOT, outside the context,
# where no pattern in this file can reach it. Adding those four would read as four more
# guarantees and be four inert lines, which is the exact failure the heading above was
# written to stop doing. The model-weights class is absent for a different reason: it is a
# SCOPE matter rather than a credential one, and `*.bin` would deny a wasm or font asset
# under `public/` that a portal may legitimately ship.
#
# `**/*credential*` subsumes `credentials.json` and `*-credentials*`. Both are kept anyway,
# against this file's own "two spellings of one rule invite an edit to half of it" warning,
# because the gate enforcing this set compares LINES: a reader who deletes a subsumed line
# should be told rather than quietly agreed with. The gate resolves that tension; this
# comment only records it.
**/*.env
**/secrets/
**/.secrets/
**/*.secret
**/*.secrets
**/credentials.json
**/*credential*
**/*-credentials*
**/auth.json
**/.sops.yaml
**/.sops/
**/*.kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig.*
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa.*
**/id_ed25519.*
**/*.ppk
**/known_hosts
**/*.token
**/_netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
